In cloud environments, stable connectivity is essential. That’s where Elastic IP comes in.
An Elastic IP is a static public IPv4 address designed for dynamic cloud computing. Unlike normal public IPs, it stays associated with your AWS account and can be quickly remapped to another instance whenever needed.

 Key Benefits:
 • Provides a permanent public IP address for your cloud resources
 • Maintains consistent access to applications and servers
 • Supports quick failover by reassigning the IP to another instance
 • Commonly used for web servers, NAT gateways, and production workloads
In simple terms, Elastic IP helps keep your applications reachable even when infrastructure changes. 
